                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_32\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds a missing \"left\" string to an alignment array in\nInstructorDetailAction.java, changing:\n    new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\"},\nto:\n    new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\", \"left\"},\nThis array is the third constructor argument of the WebTable used to render\nthe \"no committed timetable yet\" branch of the instructor's class-assignment\ntable, and it must have exactly as many entries as the header-label array\n(the second constructor argument) and the WebTable's declared column count\n(the first constructor argument), otherwise the WebTable code indexes past\nthe end of the array and throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.\n\nTracing this exact code block through the candidates:\n- candidate_01 first introduces the block with 5 columns, 5 headers, and a\n  matching 5-element alignment array (balanced).\n- candidate_06 and candidate_09 change header text/count but keep the\n  alignment array in sync (still balanced).\n- candidate_21 and candidate_26 similarly add columns to the \"hasTimetable\"\n  branch while leaving the untouched \"else\" branch (5 columns / 5 headers /\n  5 aligns) balanced.\n- candidate_32 changes the \"else\" branch from `new WebTable( 5, ...)` to\n  `new WebTable( 6, ...)` and adds `MSG.columnTeachingResponsibility()` to\n  the header array (making it 6 header labels: Class, Check Conflicts,\n  Share, Teaching Responsibility, Limit, Manager), but does NOT add a\n  corresponding 6th entry to the alignment array, which is left at:\n      new String[] {\"left\", \"left\",\"left\", \"left\", \"left\"},\n  (only 5 elements). This mismatch (6 declared columns / 6 headers / 5\n  alignment strings) is precisely the bug that causes the\n  ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException described in the fix commit message,\n  which occurs when an instructor is assigned to classes but there is no\n  committed timetable yet (i.e., exactly the \"else\" branch built in\n  candidate_32).\n- candidate_33 modifies nearby code (icon/conflict highlighting) but does\n  not touch this array at all, so the bug persists unchanged.\n- candidate_34 is the fix itself, adding the missing \"left\" to restore the\n  5-vs-6 balance, exactly matching fix_commit_diff.txt.\n\nBecause candidate_32 is the commit that first created the 6-vs-5 mismatch\nbetween the header array and the alignment array in the no-timetable\nbranch, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
